1. Flight in bats is an analogous adaptation (convergent evolution) achieved through a skin membrane (patagium) stretched between elongated finger bones, NOT modified forelimb feathers as in birds.
2. Bats exhibit true mammalian characteristics:
   (a) Possess **mammary glands** to nurse their young with milk;
   (b) Body is covered with **hair/fur** rather than feathers;
   (c) Possess **external ear pinnae** and heterodont teeth;
   (d) They are **viviparous**, giving birth to live young rather than laying eggs.

1. **Organism**: The **Purple Frog** (*Nasikabatrachus sahyadrensis*), endemic to the Western Ghats of India.
2. **Adaptations**:
   (a) Bloated, dark purple rounded body with exceptionally short, muscular limbs for subterranean burrowing;
   (b) Hard spade-like tubercle on hind feet used like a shovel to burrow backwards deep into wet soil;
   (c) Pointed snout with a narrow mouth specialized for eating underground termites;
   (d) Spends ~50 weeks of the year buried up to 3 meters underground, emerging only for roughly 2 weeks during monsoon rains to mate in temporary streams.
